From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:32:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 17/45] inkling2: serve images through the two-rank engine

With --vision on both ranks, rank 0 loads the tower from the pack's
vision.safetensors and encodes each request's pictures before its
prompt's first pass. The rows reach rank 1 by NCCL broadcast and are
spliced right after the embedding in prompt passes only.

A picture may take 4096 visual tokens at most, and larger ones are
refused with a message naming the limit. Image prompts are never kept
in or resumed from the prompt cache, because every picture shares one
placeholder id.
